{
  "description": "Deterministic resolution vectors for selection-dependent price_adjustments on binding fixed-price pricing options. Each resolution case names a declared option and the buyer's concrete selections, and asserts the resolved fixed_price, the ordered rows that fire, and each fired row's currency amount. Rules under test: matching is full-identity equality across encodings; per dimension at most one row fires (the first matching row in declared order); stacking is additive against the base rate (each delta is computed from fixed_price, never from another row, so cross-dimension order does not change the price); each rate delta is rounded half away from zero to the option's price precision (greatest of the currency minor-unit exponent, 4 for cpm/vcpm/cpc/cpcv/cpv, and the fewest decimal places that exactly represent fixed_price and each amount, by numeric value); the resolved price is the exact sum and never below zero. Arithmetic MUST be exact decimal or integer.",
  "currency_minor_unit_exponent": {
    "USD": 2,
    "JPY": 0
  },
